  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 13,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 305.162, 435.192, 557.189, 524.063 ],
    "font" : "MinionPro-Regular",
    "font size" : 8.8,
    "text color" : "[0.75, 0.68, 0.67, 0.902]",
    "content" : " e kit supplies su cient materials for performing 1000 assays based on a 200 µL sample volume or a proportionately lower number of assays with a larger sample volume.  e CyQUANT® cell-lysis bu er (a 20X concentrate, C7027) is also available separately and has been formulated to produce e cient lysis, to protect nucleic acids from nuclease activity and to dissociate proteins that may interfere with dye binding to nucleic acids. It may prove generally useful in the development of other assays that require cell lysis."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 14,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 305.162, 413.735, 481.845, 426.356 ],
    "font" : "MyriadPro-Regular",
    "font size" : 10.5,
    "text color" : "[0.431, 1.0, 0.432, 0.277]",
    "content" : "CyQUANT® NF Cell Proliferation Assay Kit"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 15,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 305.158, 259.192, 557.185, 414.063 ],
    "font" : "MinionPro-Regular",
    "font size" : 8.8,
    "text color" : "[0.75, 0.68, 0.67, 0.902]",
    "content" : " e CyQUANT® NF Cell Proliferation Assay Kit provides a fast and sensitive method for counting cells in a population and measuring proliferation in microplate format.71  is assay can be completed in 1 hour, with no washes, cell lysis, long incubations or radioactivity required, and it is not dependent on physiological activities that may exhibit cell number–independent variability.  e CyQUANT® NF assay eliminates the freeze-thaw cell lysis step of the original CyQUANT® cell proliferation assay by using a cell-permeant DNA-binding dye in combination with a plasma membrane–permeabilization reagent.  e CyQUANT® NF assay protocol requires only aspiration of growth medium (for adherent cells), replacement with dye binding solution, incubation for 30–60 minutes and then measurement of  uorescence in a microplate reader.  e CyQUANT® NF assay has a linear detection range from at least 100 to 20,000 cells per well in most cell lines using a 96-well microplate format and a 100 µL assay volume."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 16,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 305.153, 215.192, 557.157, 260.063 ],
    "font" : "MinionPro-Regular",
    "font size" : 8.8,
    "text color" : "[0.75, 0.68, 0.67, 0.902]",
    "content" : " e CyQUANT® NF Cell Proliferation Assay Kit can be used with either a 96-well or 384-well microplate format and is available in two con gurations: a 200-assay kit (C35007) and a 1000-assay kit (C35006) for high-throughput applications."
  }, {
